# System-2.0 Improvements — Implementation Plan

Fix auth flow issues, critical security bugs, penalty logic, consolidate game logic, and migrate GraphQL mutations to REST.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Stat Level-Up Model — Still Need Your Answer:**
> - **A) Reset model** (subtract stat value on level-up) — stat value shows "progress toward next level"
> - **B) Cumulative model** (no subtraction) — stat value grows forever, level = milestone
>
> `questController` uses (A), sidequests/resolvers use (B). Which do you prefer?

---

## 🔴 Phase 0: Auth Overhaul + Modern Google Auth

Two problems solved together: fix the deployment auth bugs AND replace the old Passport.js redirect flow with modern Google Identity Services.

### Current Flow (Broken — 6 redirect hops)

```
Google Login button clicked
   ↓
window.location.assign('/auth/google')             ← full page redirect to server
   ↓
Passport redirects to Google consent screen         ← 2nd redirect
   ↓
Google redirects to /auth/google/callback           ← 3rd redirect
   ↓
Server redirects to /oauth-transfer?token=JWT       ← 4th redirect + TOKEN IN URL 🔴
   ↓
SetCookie.jsx POSTs token to /set-cookie            ← 5th step, another network call
   ↓
Navigate to /oauth-success                          ← 6th step
   ↓
OAuthSuccess calls useLoadUser() AGAIN              ← double fetch, race condition
   ↓
ProtectedRoute(allowGuest) sees user → redirects    ← redirect loop risk
   ↓
Finally reaches /dashboard                          ← after ~5 seconds of flashing
```

**Problems:** `passport`/`passport-google-oauth20`/`express-session` dependencies, JWT leaked in URL, 3 throwaway pages (`SetCookie`, [OAuthSuccess](file:///c:/Users/astra/Desktop/projects/System-2.0/Client/src/components/OathSuccess.jsx#6-22), [GoogleLogin](file:///c:/Users/astra/Desktop/projects/System-2.0/Client/src/pages/Login.jsx#94-98)), double [useLoadUser](file:///c:/Users/astra/Desktop/projects/System-2.0/Client/src/utils/userLoader.js#9-52), [ProtectedRoute](file:///c:/Users/astra/Desktop/projects/System-2.0/Client/src/components/ProtectedRoute.jsx#5-24) redirect loops, sequential tracker refresh blocks all pages, no `initialized` reset on logout.

### New Flow (Modern — 0 redirects)

```
Google Login button clicked
   ↓
@react-oauth/google opens popup (already installed!)
   ↓
User consents in popup, popup closes
   ↓
Client gets Google credential (ID token)
   ↓
POST /auth/google { credential }                   ← single API call
   ↓
Server verifies ID token with google-auth-library
Finds/creates user, signs JWT, sets httpOnly cookie
   ↓
Client receives { user } → setUser → navigate('/dashboard')
   ↓
Done. Zero redirects, zero intermediate pages.
```

### Backend Changes

#### [NEW] `google-auth-library` dependency
```bash
npm install google-auth-library  # replaces passport + passport-google-oauth20
```

#### [MODIFY] [authRoutes.js](file:///c:/Users/astra/Desktop/projects/System-2.0/Server/Routes/authRoutes.js)
- Remove `GET /google` and `GET /google/callback` (Passport redirect routes)
- Add `POST /auth/google` that accepts `{ credential }`, verifies with `google-auth-library`, creates/finds user, returns JWT cookie

```js
// New route (simplified)
router.post('/google', async (req, res) => {
  const { credential } = req.body;
  const ticket = await googleClient.verifyIdToken({
    idToken: credential,
    audience: process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,
  });
  const { email, name, picture } = ticket.getPayload();
  let user = await User.findOne({ email });
  if (!user) user = await User.create({ username: name, email, avatar: picture });
  const token = jwt.sign({ id: user._id }, process.env.JWT_SECRET, { expiresIn: '7d' });
  res.cookie('token', token, cookieOptions).json({ user });
});
```

#### [DELETE] [config/passport.js](file:///c:/Users/astra/Desktop/projects/System-2.0/Server/config/passport.js)
- Entire file removed (GoogleStrategy, serialize/deserialize)

